# Maze's End says "put it onto the battlefield", not tapped: a Gate with no enters-tapped text of its own (Talon Gates of Madara) arrives
# untapped and can be tapped for mana at once - unlike the Guildgates, which enter tapped by their own text (CR 614.1d). Its "up to one
# target creature phases out" enters trigger has no creature to choose.

[Bot1 Deck]
Maze's End
Mox Jet
Mox Ruby
Mox Pearl
Island x3
Island x8
Talon Gates of Madara
Island x8

[Bot2 Deck]
Island x20

[Actions]
Bot1.Hand.Maze's End.Play
Bot1.Hand.Mox Jet.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Mox Ruby.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Mox Pearl.Cast
[T3 Bot1.Main1]
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Jet.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Ruby.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Pearl.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Maze's End.Activate(Ability: Return)
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Pass
? Bot1.Hand = Island; Island; Island; Island; Maze's End
! Bot1.Search(Island)
Bot1.Search(Talon Gates of Madara)

[Expect]
Bot1.Battlefield.Talon Gates of Madara.Tapped = false
Bot1.Battlefield.Talon Gates of Madara.Subtypes = Gate
Result = InProgress
